Subject: [PATCH] pygnmi: bracket IPv6 gRPC targets without changing socket hosts

PyPI pygnmi 0.8.15 constructs the gRPC target before its IPv6 handling.
Adapt https://github.com/akarneliuk/pygnmi/pull/166 to retain the Unix socket
path and accept both bare and already-bracketed IPv6 addresses. Keep the
socket host unbracketed for automatic TLS certificate retrieval.

Related: https://github.com/akarneliuk/pygnmi/issues/179
Revalidate/remove when upgrading the pinned dependency to a corrected release.
---
 pygnmi/client.py | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pygnmi/client.py b/pygnmi/client.py
--- a/pygnmi/client.py
+++ b/pygnmi/client.py
@@ -101,7 +101,9 @@ class gNMIclient(object):
             self.__target = target
             self.__target_path = target[0]
         elif re.match(".*:.*", target[0]):
-            self.__target = (f"[{target[0]}]", target[1])
+            host = target[0].strip("[]")
+            self.__target = (host, target[1])
+            self.__target_path = f"[{host}]:{target[1]}"
         else:
             self.__target = target
